@startuml
title Forgix power-on to steady state - simplified

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor Power
participant "RP2354 boot ROM" as ROM
database "Boot flash" as Flash
control "RP2354 firmware" as MCU
participant "Trion FPGA" as FPGA
database "QSPI PSRAM" as PSRAM
boundary "USB host" as Host

Power -> ROM : Reset released

alt External 10 kOhm CS1 pull-up fitted
  ROM -> Flash : Read boot image over QSPI
  note right of PSRAM
    PSRAM CS# remains high,
    so it ignores shared-bus traffic.
  end note
else Pull-up missing on the current board
  ROM -> Flash : Attempt boot reads over shared QSPI
  PSRAM --> ROM : May also respond while CS# is pulled low
  note over ROM, PSRAM
    The boot can wedge here before firmware,
    FPGA configuration, or the analyzer trigger.
  end note
end

ROM -> MCU : Start firmware if XIP reads succeeded
MCU -> MCU : Immediately change CS1 pad to pull-up
MCU -> FPGA : Load embedded FPGA bitstream
FPGA --> MCU : CDONE high; ping returns design ID 0xB8

alt FPGA ready
  MCU -> FPGA : Set GPO0 / PIN13 high
end
MCU -> PSRAM : Run boot-only reset, identity and scratch POST
alt FPGA ready
  MCU -> FPGA : Set GPO0 / PIN13 low
end

MCU -> Host : Start USB console and print boot report

loop Steady-state foreground loop
  MCU -> MCU : Feed watchdog and service USB/UI
  MCU -> FPGA : Heartbeat updates and once-per-second health checks
end

@enduml
